1
00:00:51,018 --> 00:00:56,924
<i>In the beginning,</i>
<i>there was only ocean...</i>

2
00:01:02,263 --> 00:01:05,299
<i>until she emerged.</i>

3
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:10,137
<i>Our mother island, Te Fiti.</i>

4
00:01:11,339 --> 00:01:17,244
<i>Her heart held the power</i>
<i>to create life itself...</i>

5
00:01:18,846 --> 00:01:22,550
<i>and Te Fiti shared it</i>
<i>with the world.</i>

6
00:01:24,418 --> 00:01:29,223
<i>In time,</i>
<i>some sought to capture</i>
<i>the heart for themselves.</i>

7
00:01:29,357 --> 00:01:33,661
<i>For they believed,</i>
<i>if they could possess it,</i>

8
00:01:33,794 --> 00:01:37,565
<i>the power of creation</i>
<i>would be theirs.</i>

9
00:01:39,967 --> 00:01:43,137
<i>And one day,</i>
<i>the most daring of them all</i>

10
00:01:43,270 --> 00:01:47,641
<i>voyaged across the vast ocean</i>
<i>to take it.</i>

11
00:01:47,775 --> 00:01:51,679
<i>He was a demigod</i>
<i>of the wind and sea.</i>

12
00:01:51,812 --> 00:01:53,814
Whoo-hoo!

13
00:01:53,948 --> 00:01:55,516
<i>A warrior.</i>

14
00:01:57,084 --> 00:01:59,186
<i>A trickster.</i>

15
00:02:00,154 --> 00:02:03,190
Chee Hoo!

16
00:02:04,425 --> 00:02:07,695
<i>A shape-shifter...</i>

17
00:02:07,828 --> 00:02:09,163
<i>...who could change form</i>

18
00:02:09,296 --> 00:02:13,134
<i>with the power of</i>
<i>his magical fish hook.</i>

19
00:02:13,267 --> 00:02:17,838
<i>And his name was Maui.</i>

20
00:02:30,818 --> 00:02:32,887
She was rumbling
before we got here, right?

21
00:02:37,058 --> 00:02:39,393
<i>But without her heart,</i>

22
00:02:39,528 --> 00:02:42,563
<i>Te Fiti began to crumble,</i>

23
00:02:42,696 --> 00:02:46,100
<i>giving birth</i>
<i>to a terrible darkness.</i>

24
00:02:50,738 --> 00:02:52,507
<i>Maui tried to escape,</i>

25
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:57,178
<i>but was confronted by another</i>
<i>who sought the heart.</i>

26
00:02:58,646 --> 00:03:03,250
<i>Te Ka!</i>
<i>A demon of earth and fire.</i>

27
00:03:04,785 --> 00:03:07,121
<i>Maui was struck</i>
<i>from the sky...</i>

28
00:03:08,456 --> 00:03:11,459
<i>...never to be seen again.</i>

29
00:03:11,592 --> 00:03:16,497
<i>And his magical fish hook</i>
<i>and the heart of Te Fiti</i>

30
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:18,432
<i>were lost to the sea,</i>

31
00:03:18,567 --> 00:03:22,903
<i>where, even now,</i>
<i>a thousand years later,</i>

32
00:03:23,037 --> 00:03:25,372
<i>Te Ka</i>
<i>and the demons of the deep</i>

33
00:03:25,507 --> 00:03:28,109
<i>still hunt for the heart.</i>

34
00:03:28,242 --> 00:03:32,346
<i>Hiding in a darkness</i>
<i>that will continue to spread.</i>

35
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:37,685
<i>Draining the life</i>
<i>from island after island,</i>

36
00:03:37,818 --> 00:03:39,987
until we are all devoured

37
00:03:40,121 --> 00:03:45,860
by the bloodthirsty
inescapable jaws of death!

38
00:03:47,628 --> 00:03:51,332
But one day,
the heart will be found

39
00:03:52,166 --> 00:03:57,171
by someone who will journey
beyond our reef,

40
00:03:57,738 --> 00:03:59,974
find Maui,

41
00:04:00,107 --> 00:04:03,878
deliver him across
the great ocean

42
00:04:04,011 --> 00:04:08,015
to restore
the heart of Te Fiti

43
00:04:08,149 --> 00:04:11,886
and save us all.

44
00:04:12,019 --> 00:04:13,888
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

45
00:04:15,389 --> 00:04:17,358
Thank you, Mother.

46
00:04:17,491 --> 00:04:19,393
-Papa.
-There she is.

47
00:04:19,528 --> 00:04:23,532
As you all know,
no one goes beyond the reef.

48
00:04:23,664 --> 00:04:25,166
We are safe here.

49
00:04:25,299 --> 00:04:29,036
There is no darkness,
and there are no monsters.

50
00:04:30,471 --> 00:04:32,607
Monsters!

51
00:04:33,207 --> 00:04:35,776
I said there are no monsters.

52
00:04:39,413 --> 00:04:43,817
As long as we stay
on our very safe island,
we'll be fine.

53
00:04:43,951 --> 00:04:46,720
<i>The legends are true, Son.</i>

54
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:19,220
Don't worry. I'll help you.

55
00:05:19,353 --> 00:05:21,755
Shoo! Shoo, shoo!

56
00:05:22,356 --> 00:05:23,424
Leave him alone.

57
00:05:25,092 --> 00:05:26,927
Wanna go to the ocean?

58
00:05:27,696 --> 00:05:29,730
Yeah, me too.

59
00:05:43,444 --> 00:05:44,613
Whoa!

60
00:06:56,984 --> 00:06:58,452
Moana!

61
00:07:01,021 --> 00:07:02,256
Moana.

62
00:07:03,692 --> 00:07:05,192
Moana.

63
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:08,996
Moana, we don't go out there.

64
00:07:09,129 --> 00:07:10,931
It's dangerous.

65
00:07:15,035 --> 00:07:16,036
Moana, listen.

66
00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:17,772
There is nothing
beyond the reef

67
00:07:17,905 --> 00:07:19,206
but storms and rough seas.

68
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:20,841
-Moana.
-Mom's here.

69
00:07:20,974 --> 00:07:23,712
There's my little adventurer.

70
00:07:23,844 --> 00:07:25,846
You are very important,
sweetheart,

71
00:07:25,979 --> 00:07:28,048
and the next great chief
of our people.

72
00:07:28,182 --> 00:07:30,017
And you will do
wondrous things.

73
00:07:30,150 --> 00:07:31,653
Can I do them in the water?

74
00:07:31,786 --> 00:07:33,387
No.

75
00:07:34,955 --> 00:07:36,490
Never pass the reef.

76
00:07:36,890 --> 00:07:38,359
Come on.

77
00:07:38,492 --> 00:07:40,994
First, you must learn
where you're meant to be.

78
00:07:52,741 --> 00:07:54,108
Ah!

79
00:07:58,178 --> 00:08:02,517
♪ <i>Moana!</i>
<i>Make way! Make way!</i> ♪

80
00:08:02,650 --> 00:08:04,485
♪ <i>Moana, it's time you knew</i> ♪

81
00:08:04,619 --> 00:08:08,623
♪ <i>The village of Motunui</i>
<i>Is all you need</i> ♪

82
00:08:08,757 --> 00:08:09,890
Heihei.

83
00:08:10,023 --> 00:08:11,392
♪ <i>The dancers are practicing!</i> ♪

84
00:08:11,526 --> 00:08:13,127
♪ <i>They dance to</i>
<i>An ancient song</i> ♪

85
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:14,529
♪ <i>Who needs a new song?</i> ♪

86
00:08:14,662 --> 00:08:16,230
♪ <i>This old one's all we need</i> ♪

87
00:08:16,363 --> 00:08:17,931
♪ <i>This tradition is</i>
<i>Our mission</i> ♪

88
00:08:18,065 --> 00:08:20,835
♪ <i>And, Moana,</i>
<i>There's so much to do!</i> ♪

89
00:08:20,968 --> 00:08:24,639
♪ <i>Don't trip on the taro root</i>
<i>That's all you need</i> ♪

90
00:08:24,773 --> 00:08:26,608
♪ <i>We share</i>
<i>Everything we make</i> ♪

91
00:08:26,741 --> 00:08:28,208
♪ <i>We make</i> ♪

92
00:08:28,342 --> 00:08:29,811
♪ <i>We joke</i>
<i>And we weave our baskets</i> ♪

93
00:08:29,943 --> 00:08:31,311
♪ <i>The fishermen</i>
<i>Come back from the sea</i> ♪

94
00:08:31,445 --> 00:08:33,147
♪ <i>I wanna see</i> ♪

95
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:34,749
♪ <i>Don't walk away</i> ♪

96
00:08:34,883 --> 00:08:36,851
♪ <i>Moana,</i>
<i>Stay on the ground now</i> ♪

97
00:08:36,984 --> 00:08:39,219
♪ <i>Our people will need</i>
<i>A chief and</i> ♪

98
00:08:39,353 --> 00:08:41,321
<i>- </i> ♪ <i>There you are</i> ♪
- ♪ <i>There you are</i> ♪

99
00:08:41,455 --> 00:08:43,257
♪ <i>There comes a day</i> ♪

100
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:45,325
♪ <i>When you're gonna</i>
<i>Look around</i> ♪

101
00:08:45,459 --> 00:08:47,094
♪ <i>And realize happiness is</i> ♪

102
00:08:47,227 --> 00:08:49,163
♪ <i>Where you are</i> ♪

103
00:08:49,296 --> 00:08:51,398
<i>-</i> ♪ <i>Consider the coconut!</i> ♪
<i>-</i> ♪ <i>The what?</i> ♪

104
00:08:51,533 --> 00:08:53,501
♪ <i>Consider its tree</i> ♪

105
00:08:53,635 --> 00:08:57,404
♪ <i>Use each part of the coconut</i>
<i>It's all we need</i> ♪

106
00:08:57,539 --> 00:08:59,507
♪ <i>We make our nets</i>
<i>From the fibers</i> ♪

107
00:08:59,641 --> 00:09:01,375
♪ <i>The water is sweet inside</i> ♪

108
00:09:01,509 --> 00:09:03,310
♪ <i>We use the leaves</i>
<i>To build fires</i> ♪

109
00:09:03,444 --> 00:09:05,513
♪ <i>And cook up</i>
<i>The meat inside</i> ♪

110
00:09:05,647 --> 00:09:09,316
♪ <i>Consider the coconuts!</i>
<i>The trunks and the leaves!</i> ♪

111
00:09:09,450 --> 00:09:12,319
♪ <i>The island gives us</i>
<i>What we need</i> ♪

112
00:09:12,453 --> 00:09:14,054
♪ <i>And no one leaves</i> ♪

113
00:09:14,188 --> 00:09:15,857
♪ <i>That's right, we stay</i> ♪

114
00:09:15,989 --> 00:09:17,625
♪ <i>We're safe</i>
<i>And we're well-provided</i> ♪

115
00:09:17,759 --> 00:09:19,794
♪ <i>And when we look to</i>
<i>The future</i> ♪

116
00:09:19,928 --> 00:09:22,262
♪ <i>There you are</i> ♪

117
00:09:22,396 --> 00:09:23,932
♪ <i>She'll be okay</i> ♪

118
00:09:24,064 --> 00:09:25,966
♪ <i>In time, she'll learn</i>
<i>Just as I did</i> ♪

119
00:09:26,099 --> 00:09:32,172
♪ <i>You must find happiness</i>
<i>Right where you are</i> ♪

120
00:09:32,306 --> 00:09:34,141
♪ <i>I like to dance</i>
<i>With the water</i> ♪

121
00:09:34,274 --> 00:09:36,210
♪ <i>The undertow and the waves</i> ♪

122
00:09:36,343 --> 00:09:40,447
♪ <i>The water is mischievous, ha!</i>
<i>I like how it misbehaves</i> ♪

123
00:09:40,582 --> 00:09:42,550
♪ <i>Some people</i>
<i>May think I'm crazy</i> ♪

124
00:09:42,684 --> 00:09:45,285
♪ <i>Or say that</i>
<i>I drift too far</i> ♪

125
00:09:45,419 --> 00:09:46,754
♪ <i>But once you know</i>
<i>What you like</i> ♪

126
00:09:46,888 --> 00:09:50,658
♪ <i>Well, there you are</i> ♪

127
00:09:56,731 --> 00:09:59,366
♪ <i>You are</i>
<i>Your father's daughter</i> ♪

128
00:09:59,501 --> 00:10:01,401
♪ <i>Stubbornness and pride</i> ♪

129
00:10:01,536 --> 00:10:03,671
♪ <i>Mind what he says</i>
<i>But remember</i> ♪

130
00:10:03,805 --> 00:10:05,974
♪ <i>You may hear</i>
<i>A voice inside</i> ♪

131
00:10:06,106 --> 00:10:08,810
♪ <i>And if that voice</i>
<i>Starts to whisper</i> ♪

132
00:10:08,943 --> 00:10:11,311
♪ <i>To follow</i>
<i>The farthest star</i> ♪

133
00:10:11,445 --> 00:10:17,619
♪ <i>Moana, that voice inside</i>
<i>Is who you are</i> ♪

134
00:10:34,067 --> 00:10:35,302
Moana.

135
00:10:35,435 --> 00:10:37,471
Dad. I wasn't gonna
go out there.

136
00:10:37,605 --> 00:10:40,808
Just doing my daily
canoe inspections.

137
00:10:42,175 --> 00:10:43,611
Walk with me.

138
00:10:47,314 --> 00:10:51,351
I wanted to bring you here
since the moment
you opened your eyes.

139
00:10:51,886 --> 00:10:54,388
This is a sacred place.

140
00:10:56,323 --> 00:10:58,560
A place of chiefs.

141
00:10:59,326 --> 00:11:01,663
Soon you will come of age,

142
00:11:01,796 --> 00:11:05,098
and place a stone
on this mountain like I did.

143
00:11:05,967 --> 00:11:07,502
Like my father did.

144
00:11:08,368 --> 00:11:10,470
And his mother did.

145
00:11:10,605 --> 00:11:12,874
And every chief
that has ever been.

146
00:11:13,775 --> 00:11:16,410
And on that day,
when you add your stone...

147
00:11:17,712 --> 00:11:21,049
you will raise
this whole island higher.

148
00:11:21,849 --> 00:11:24,652
You are the future of
our people, Moana.

149
00:11:25,385 --> 00:11:28,088
And our people
are not out there.

150
00:11:28,957 --> 00:11:30,625
They're right here.

151
00:11:30,758 --> 00:11:34,394
It's time to start preparing
to be who they need you to be.

152
00:11:44,171 --> 00:11:45,873
♪ <i>We make our nets</i>
<i>From the fibers</i> ♪

153
00:11:46,007 --> 00:11:47,542
♪ <i>We weave our nets</i>
<i>From the fibers</i> ♪

154
00:11:47,675 --> 00:11:49,577
♪ <i>A real tasty treat inside</i> ♪

155
00:11:49,711 --> 00:11:51,278
♪ <i>We sing these songs</i>
<i>In our choirs</i> ♪

156
00:11:51,411 --> 00:11:53,280
♪ <i>We have</i>
<i>Mouths to feed inside</i> ♪

157
00:11:53,413 --> 00:11:54,616
-♪ <i>The village believes in us</i> ♪
-♪ <i>That's right</i> ♪

158
00:11:54,749 --> 00:11:56,350
♪ <i>The village believes</i> ♪

159
00:11:56,483 --> 00:11:58,686
♪ <i>The island gives us</i>
<i>What we need</i> ♪

160
00:11:58,820 --> 00:12:00,387
♪ <i>And no one leaves</i> ♪

161
00:12:00,521 --> 00:12:02,255
♪ <i>So here I'll stay</i> ♪

162
00:12:02,389 --> 00:12:04,626
♪ <i>My home, my people</i>
<i>Beside me</i> ♪

163
00:12:04,759 --> 00:12:08,963
♪ <i>And when I think of tomorrow</i>
<i>There we are</i> ♪

164
00:12:09,097 --> 00:12:10,565
♪ <i>I'll lead the way</i> ♪

165
00:12:10,698 --> 00:12:12,667
♪ <i>I'll have my people</i>
<i>To guide me</i> ♪

166
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:16,738
♪ <i>We'll build our future</i>
<i>Together, where we are</i> ♪

167
00:12:16,871 --> 00:12:18,438
♪ <i>'Cause every path</i>
<i>Leads you back to</i> ♪

168
00:12:18,573 --> 00:12:20,608
♪ <i>Where you are</i> ♪

169
00:12:20,742 --> 00:12:24,646
♪ <i>You can find happiness</i>
<i>Right where you are</i> ♪

170
00:12:24,779 --> 00:12:31,819
♪ <i>Where you are</i>
<i>Where you are</i> ♪

171
00:12:32,185 --> 00:12:34,722
Chee Hoo!

172
00:12:38,026 --> 00:12:40,662
Yeah, yeah. Pull it.

173
00:12:41,228 --> 00:12:42,563
Pull it tight.

174
00:12:48,069 --> 00:12:50,705
Careful, Heihei. Stay.

175
00:12:53,574 --> 00:12:55,576
Pua!

176
00:12:58,412 --> 00:12:59,814
Thank you very much.

177
00:13:06,554 --> 00:13:09,389
We need to review the meaning
of the word "stay."

178
00:13:38,318 --> 00:13:39,620
All right.

179
00:13:39,754 --> 00:13:41,622
Let's give this stone thing
a try, Pua.

180
00:13:41,756 --> 00:13:44,826
This one says "passionate."

181
00:13:49,997 --> 00:13:51,498
Which grove?

182
00:13:51,632 --> 00:13:53,300
Over there.

183
00:13:53,433 --> 00:13:54,702
It's getting worse.

184
00:13:54,836 --> 00:13:56,938
We should clear
any diseased trees.

185
00:13:57,071 --> 00:13:59,574
Replant. Let us know
if you find more.

186
00:14:00,575 --> 00:14:03,410
"Leader of the people."

187
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:09,584
This is "playful, but fierce."

188
00:14:12,553 --> 00:14:14,021
It's important, Pua.

189
00:14:18,325 --> 00:14:19,994
It's forever.

190
00:14:20,128 --> 00:14:22,163
None of those boats have fish.

191
00:14:22,295 --> 00:14:23,731
We checked everywhere.

192
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,503
-I looked over there.
-We need to let the chief...

193
00:14:28,636 --> 00:14:30,204
What's wrong?

194
00:14:30,337 --> 00:14:33,708
It's not just the coconuts now,
it's also the catch.

195
00:14:34,474 --> 00:14:36,511
We've tried the whole lagoon.

196
00:14:37,078 --> 00:14:38,713
There are no fish.

197
00:14:39,247 --> 00:14:41,348
They are just gone.

198
00:14:43,985 --> 00:14:46,721
I remember when
my grandmother was chief.

199
00:14:46,854 --> 00:14:49,690
A hurricane
kept the fish away for weeks.

200
00:14:49,824 --> 00:14:53,161
But they had dried fish stores
and fresh coconuts.

201
00:14:53,293 --> 00:14:56,931
They were prepared to wait
until the fish came back.

202
00:14:57,064 --> 00:14:59,133
And they did come back.

203
00:14:59,267 --> 00:15:01,035
But there is no hurricane.

204
00:15:01,169 --> 00:15:04,238
And even then,
the lagoon was never empty.

205
00:15:04,371 --> 00:15:07,875
There's always a solution.
We just need to look for it.

206
00:15:08,009 --> 00:15:09,610
Ow!

207
00:15:17,618 --> 00:15:19,386
If the lagoon is empty,

208
00:15:20,154 --> 00:15:22,690
what if...
what if we fish farther out?

209
00:15:23,157 --> 00:15:24,225
Beyond the reef.

210
00:15:26,861 --> 00:15:28,328
No one goes beyond the reef.

211
00:15:28,461 --> 00:15:29,897
But if we can't
rely on coconuts

212
00:15:30,031 --> 00:15:31,566
-and the fish here are gone...
-Moana.

213
00:15:31,699 --> 00:15:33,234
...and we're surrounded by
a whole ocean.

214
00:15:33,366 --> 00:15:34,902
We have one rule.

215
00:15:35,036 --> 00:15:37,038
-A rule when there was food.
-A rule that keeps us safe.

216
00:15:37,171 --> 00:15:38,206
We have to do something.

217
00:15:38,338 --> 00:15:40,875
I will not endanger our people

218
00:15:41,008 --> 00:15:43,711
so you can run
back to the water.

219
00:16:03,965 --> 00:16:05,099
Moana.

220
00:16:05,967 --> 00:16:08,236
I thought I'd find you here.

221
00:16:08,368 --> 00:16:10,738
I didn't say
we should go beyond the reef

222
00:16:10,872 --> 00:16:12,940
because I wanna be
on the ocean.

223
00:16:13,341 --> 00:16:14,609
I know.

224
00:16:15,576 --> 00:16:17,778
But you kind of do.

225
00:16:19,213 --> 00:16:21,983
I am trying to be
what our people need.

226
00:16:22,482 --> 00:16:23,784
What he needs.

227
00:16:23,918 --> 00:16:26,419
But it doesn't seem to be
enough for him.

228
00:16:27,955 --> 00:16:30,124
He was just like you, Moana.

229
