<i>What a terrible performance</i> ♪

944
01:07:58,980 --> 01:08:00,581
♪ <i>Get the hook!</i>
<i>Get it?</i> ♪

945
01:08:00,715 --> 01:08:03,784
♪ <i>You don't swing it</i>
<i>Like you used to, man</i> ♪

946
01:08:03,918 --> 01:08:06,787
♪ <i>Yet I have to give you</i>
<i>Credit for my start</i> ♪

947
01:08:06,921 --> 01:08:10,024
♪ <i>And your tattoos</i>
<i>On the outside</i> ♪

948
01:08:10,157 --> 01:08:11,826
♪ <i>For just like you</i> ♪

949
01:08:11,959 --> 01:08:13,728
♪ <i>I've made myself</i>
<i>A work of art</i> ♪

950
01:08:13,861 --> 01:08:16,931
♪ <i>I'll never hide</i>
<i>I can't, I'm too shiny!</i> ♪

951
01:08:17,064 --> 01:08:20,067
♪ <i>Watch me dazzle</i>
<i>Like a diamond in the rough</i> ♪

952
01:08:20,201 --> 01:08:23,471
♪ <i>Strut my stuff</i>
<i>My stuff is so shiny</i> ♪

953
01:08:23,604 --> 01:08:26,407
♪ <i>Send your armies</i>
<i>But they'll never be enough</i> ♪

954
01:08:26,540 --> 01:08:29,510
♪ <i>My shell's too tough</i>
<i>Maui man</i> ♪

955
01:08:29,643 --> 01:08:31,145
♪ <i>You can try, try, try</i> ♪

956
01:08:31,278 --> 01:08:32,980
♪ <i>But you can't expect</i>
<i>A demigod</i> ♪

957
01:08:33,114 --> 01:08:34,849
♪ <i>To beat a decapod</i> ♪

958
01:08:34,982 --> 01:08:36,083
♪ <i>Look it up</i> ♪

959
01:08:36,217 --> 01:08:37,952
♪ <i>You will die, die, die</i> ♪

960
01:08:38,085 --> 01:08:40,154
♪ <i>Now it's time for me</i>
<i>To take apart</i> ♪

961
01:08:40,287 --> 01:08:42,023
♪ <i>Your aching heart</i> ♪

962
01:08:42,156 --> 01:08:46,994
♪ <i>Far from the ones</i>
<i>Who abandoned you</i> ♪

963
01:08:47,128 --> 01:08:51,699
♪ <i>Chasing the love</i>
<i>Of these humans</i> ♪

964
01:08:51,832 --> 01:08:55,002
♪ <i>Who made you feel wanted</i> ♪

965
01:08:55,136 --> 01:08:57,838
♪ <i>You tried to be tough</i> ♪

966
01:08:57,972 --> 01:09:01,609
♪ <i>But your armor's</i>
<i>Just not hard enough</i> ♪

967
01:09:01,742 --> 01:09:06,380
♪ <i>Maui, and now it's time</i>
<i>To kick your heinie</i> ♪

968
01:09:06,515 --> 01:09:09,450
♪ <i>Ever seen someone</i>
<i>So shiny...</i> ♪

969
01:09:09,583 --> 01:09:12,453
♪ <i>Soak it in cuz it's the last</i>
<i>You'll ever see</i> ♪

970
01:09:12,586 --> 01:09:15,923
♪ <i>C'est la vie, mon ami</i>
<i>I'm so shiny</i> ♪

971
01:09:16,057 --> 01:09:19,560
♪ <i>Now I eat you</i>
<i>So prepare your final plea</i> ♪

972
01:09:19,693 --> 01:09:21,328
♪ <i>Just for me</i> ♪

973
01:09:21,462 --> 01:09:24,498
♪ <i>You'll never be</i>
<i>Quite as shiny</i> ♪

974
01:09:24,632 --> 01:09:29,670
♪ <i>You wish</i>
<i>You were nice 'n' shiny</i> ♪

975
01:09:31,506 --> 01:09:33,107
-Hey!
-Huh?

976
01:09:34,909 --> 01:09:36,577
I got something shiny for ya.

977
01:09:36,710 --> 01:09:38,547
The heart of Te Fiti.

978
01:09:38,679 --> 01:09:39,647
Don't give it to him, kid.

979
01:09:39,780 --> 01:09:42,616
You want it? Come and get it.

980
01:09:42,750 --> 01:09:45,753
You can't run from me.

981
01:09:45,886 --> 01:09:48,789
Oh, you can.
You keep surprising me.

982
01:09:51,192 --> 01:09:54,795
There's only so far you can
get on those two little legs.

983
01:09:54,929 --> 01:09:56,030
You tripped.

984
01:09:56,163 --> 01:09:58,866
Bad luck.

985
01:09:58,999 --> 01:10:03,070
Oh, the power of creation
for a crustacean.

986
01:10:03,204 --> 01:10:07,408
Oh.
Where is it? Where is it?

987
01:10:08,676 --> 01:10:10,778
Come on, Te Fiti.

988
01:10:10,911 --> 01:10:13,515
Time to go. Shall we?

989
01:10:13,647 --> 01:10:15,483
-What about the heart?
-He can have it.

990
01:10:15,616 --> 01:10:16,917
I've got a better one.

991
01:10:17,051 --> 01:10:20,087
Yes! It is mine! It's...

992
01:10:20,221 --> 01:10:21,055
Wait a minute.

993
01:10:21,188 --> 01:10:23,057
I see, she's taken a barnacle

994
01:10:23,190 --> 01:10:27,161
and she's covered it
in bioluminescent algae
as a diversion.

995
01:10:28,563 --> 01:10:30,831
-Come back here!
-Over there!

996
01:10:31,665 --> 01:10:33,667
There is no escape.

997
01:10:33,801 --> 01:10:36,837
- And jump!
- Chee Hoo!

998
01:10:36,971 --> 01:10:38,706
Oh, there is one escape.

999
01:10:38,839 --> 01:10:40,274
Hey, did you like the song?

1000
01:10:40,407 --> 01:10:42,776
Did you have any notes
or feedback?

1001
01:10:52,887 --> 01:10:55,856
Maui. Maui.

1002
01:10:58,792 --> 01:11:00,361
Ma--

1003
01:11:00,494 --> 01:11:03,931
Listen, I, uh,
really appreciate
what you did down there.

1004
01:11:04,064 --> 01:11:06,133
That took guts. And I...

1005
01:11:06,800 --> 01:11:08,402
Oh. I get it.

1006
01:11:08,537 --> 01:11:10,905
Big, tough,
handsome guy gets emotional.

1007
01:11:11,038 --> 01:11:13,874
And what do you do?
You laugh in his face.

1008
01:11:14,008 --> 01:11:16,343
It's just you...
you got this like...

1009
01:11:16,477 --> 01:11:18,946
Oh, no.
Is there something on my face?

1010
01:11:19,079 --> 01:11:21,749
In my teeth? Is there
something in my teeth?

1011
01:11:21,882 --> 01:11:24,385
No, no. No, no, no.
Shark head.

1012
01:11:24,519 --> 01:11:27,321
I-I like this part. I mean...
I mean the nice part.

1013
01:11:27,454 --> 01:11:30,858
I-I was not making fun
of the shark portion.

1014
01:11:30,991 --> 01:11:34,495
Look, the point is
you did me a solid.

1015
01:11:34,629 --> 01:11:36,297
But you almost died.

1016
01:11:36,430 --> 01:11:38,365
And I couldn't even beat
the dumb crab.

1017
01:11:38,499 --> 01:11:41,636
So, chances of beating Te Ka
are bubkes.

1018
01:11:41,769 --> 01:11:45,640
This mission has no chance
because you're still you

1019
01:11:45,773 --> 01:11:47,241
and I have a shark head.

1020
01:11:49,578 --> 01:11:52,179
♪ <i>Hey, it's okay, it's okay</i> ♪

1021
01:11:52,313 --> 01:11:54,516
♪ <i>There's no wind</i> ♪

1022
01:11:54,649 --> 01:11:58,953
♪ <i>We're dead soon</i>
<i>We're dead soon</i> ♪

1023
01:11:59,086 --> 01:12:03,658
♪ <i>'Cause we're both gonna die</i>
<i>On this boat, hey</i> ♪

1024
01:12:03,791 --> 01:12:06,126
Maybe try it with a smile.

1025
01:12:06,528 --> 01:12:08,162
Giant hawk.

1026
01:12:13,901 --> 01:12:17,871
♪ <i>Maui's gonna do</i>
<i>The dead man's float, hey</i> ♪

1027
01:12:18,005 --> 01:12:19,206
Why are you being like this?

1028
01:12:19,340 --> 01:12:21,842
Leave me alone.

1029
01:12:25,746 --> 01:12:27,348
Both of you, leave me alone.

1030
01:12:30,884 --> 01:12:33,921
How do you get your tattoos?

1031
01:12:34,054 --> 01:12:37,758
They just show up...
when I earn 'em.

1032
01:12:38,459 --> 01:12:39,728
They just show up.

1033
01:12:39,860 --> 01:12:42,162
How did you get that one?

1034
01:12:44,265 --> 01:12:46,166
That one's man's
discovery of Nunya.

1035
01:12:46,300 --> 01:12:47,835
-What's Nunya?
-Nunya business.

1036
01:12:47,968 --> 01:12:50,004
-I'm just gonna keep asking.
-Drop it.

1037
01:12:50,137 --> 01:12:51,105
Why was that crab
poking at it?

1038
01:12:51,238 --> 01:12:52,139
-Back off.
-What is it?

1039
01:12:52,273 --> 01:12:53,575
-No.
-What is it?

1040
01:12:53,708 --> 01:12:55,577
-I don't want to talk about it.
-Give it back!

1041
01:13:09,423 --> 01:13:12,459
If you don't want to talk,
that's fine.

1042
01:13:13,994 --> 01:13:17,031
But my island, my people...

1043
01:13:18,767 --> 01:13:20,334
my family...

1044
01:13:22,671 --> 01:13:25,072
they won't survive
if we don't make it.

1045
01:13:26,675 --> 01:13:28,208
I want to help.

1046
01:13:29,443 --> 01:13:30,944
If you let me.

1047
01:13:44,358 --> 01:13:46,393
I wasn't born a demigod.

1048
01:13:50,632 --> 01:13:52,333
I had human parents.

1049
01:13:53,635 --> 01:13:55,369
Who decided
they didn't want me.

1050
01:13:58,172 --> 01:14:01,342
So they threw me in the ocean,
like I was nothing.

1051
01:14:02,042 --> 01:14:04,278
Somehow, I washed ashore.

1052
01:14:05,479 --> 01:14:06,947
Found by the gods.

1053
01:14:08,182 --> 01:14:09,883
They gave me my hook.

1054
01:14:10,752 --> 01:14:12,419
They made me Maui.

1055
01:14:13,320 --> 01:14:16,056
So back to the humans I went.

1056
01:14:16,857 --> 01:14:18,526
I gave them everything.

1057
01:14:19,493 --> 01:14:20,894
Islands,

1058
01:14:22,329 --> 01:14:23,565
fire,

1059
01:14:25,099 --> 01:14:26,501
coconuts.

1060
01:14:28,703 --> 01:14:31,238
I gave them
anything they ever wanted.

1061
01:14:32,774 --> 01:14:35,376
You took the heart for us.

1062
01:14:37,277 --> 01:14:39,581
You did everything for us.

1063
01:14:40,948 --> 01:14:42,316
So we'd love you.

1064
01:14:45,018 --> 01:14:46,253
Yes.

1065
01:14:49,323 --> 01:14:50,525
It was never enough.

1066
01:14:50,658 --> 01:14:53,460
The ocean chose you too.

1067
01:14:53,595 --> 01:14:55,129
That's your takeaway?

1068
01:14:55,262 --> 01:14:58,867
Because it saw someone
worthy of being saved.

1069
01:14:58,999 --> 01:15:00,134
And what am I now?

1070
01:15:00,267 --> 01:15:01,669
You're Maui.

1071
01:15:03,003 --> 01:15:05,305
The gods
didn't make that true.

1072
01:15:06,574 --> 01:15:07,975
You did.

1073
01:15:10,177 --> 01:15:12,146
Okay.

1074
01:15:13,013 --> 01:15:15,916
Okay.
Not in front of the guest.

1075
01:15:24,992 --> 01:15:27,127
The wind.

1076
01:15:27,762 --> 01:15:29,363
Maui, it's back.

1077
01:15:50,217 --> 01:15:51,519
Sorry, chicken.

1078
01:16:34,696 --> 01:16:35,663
Chee Hoo.

1079
01:18:15,029 --> 01:18:16,864
I figured it out.

1080
01:18:20,768 --> 01:18:23,671
You know, the ocean would love
when I would pull up
the islands.

1081
01:18:23,805 --> 01:18:27,542
Your ancestors would voyage
her seas and find them.

1082
01:18:27,675 --> 01:18:30,878
That necklace you're wearing,
that belonged to Tautaivasa,

1083
01:18:31,012 --> 01:18:33,113
the first master wayfinder.

1084
01:18:33,246 --> 01:18:35,349
He knew no two voyages
were the same.

1085
01:18:35,482 --> 01:18:36,784
Different every time.

1086
01:18:38,285 --> 01:18:39,787
A true wayfinder...

1087
01:18:40,855 --> 01:18:45,660
will see all the water...
as a bridge...

1088
01:18:47,461 --> 01:18:48,696
and not a barrier.

1089
01:18:50,364 --> 01:18:52,399
And if I were the ocean,

1090
01:18:53,635 --> 01:18:56,938
I couldn't find
a better curly-haired,

1091
01:18:57,071 --> 01:18:59,807
sidekick-having
non-princess...

1092
01:19:03,343 --> 01:19:05,278
...to start voyaging again.

1093
01:19:05,412 --> 01:19:09,216
That is the nicest thing
you've ever said to me.

1094
01:19:09,349 --> 01:19:11,485
Probably should've saved it
for Te Fiti.

1095
01:19:11,986 --> 01:19:13,220
I did.

1096
01:19:27,101 --> 01:19:29,704
-Moana, if I don't--
-You can do this.

1097
01:19:30,071 --> 01:19:31,304
You're Maui.

1098
01:19:34,374 --> 01:19:35,610
That's true.

1099
01:19:53,493 --> 01:19:55,429
It's Maui time.

1100
01:19:55,997 --> 01:19:57,632
Go save the world.

1101
01:19:59,734 --> 01:20:01,334
Chee Hoo!

1102
01:20:21,689 --> 01:20:22,890
Maui!

1103
01:20:44,545 --> 01:20:45,780
Maui.

1104
01:20:50,885 --> 01:20:53,487
We need to pull back. Now!

1105
01:20:57,892 --> 01:21:00,695
-What are you doing?
-Finding you a way in.

1106
01:21:01,129 --> 01:21:02,697
Now's our chance.

1107
01:21:03,531 --> 01:21:04,799
-Turn around.
-No.

1108
01:21:04,932 --> 01:21:06,433
-We're not gonna make it.
-Yes, we will.

1109
01:21:06,567 --> 01:21:08,970
-Moana, stop!
-No! I can do it.

1110
01:21:41,269 --> 01:21:42,637
Are you okay?

1111
01:21:43,504 --> 01:21:44,437
Maui?

1112
01:21:44,572 --> 01:21:46,007
I told you to turn back.

1113
01:21:46,974 --> 01:21:49,342
-I thought we could make it.
-"We"?

1114
01:21:54,816 --> 01:21:56,584
I thought I could make it.

1115
01:22:12,533 --> 01:22:13,968
I'll find a way
to fix your hook.

1116
01:22:14,101 --> 01:22:16,304
The gods made my hook.

1117
01:22:16,436 --> 01:22:18,471
You can't fix it.

1118
01:22:18,606 --> 01:22:19,941
Next time
I'll be more careful.

1119
01:22:20,074 --> 01:22:21,876
-There's no next time.
-But now we know

1120
01:22:22,009 --> 01:22:23,678
Te Ka can't follow us
into the water.

1121
01:22:23,811 --> 01:22:25,179
We can find
another way around.

1122
01:22:25,313 --> 01:22:27,882
There is no other way.
I'm not going back.

1123
01:22:28,015 --> 01:22:30,618
Take a look at my hook.
One more hit and it's over.

1124
01:22:30,751 --> 01:22:33,020
But my people, my island...

1125
01:22:33,154 --> 01:22:35,756
Without my hook,

1126
01:22:36,423 --> 01:22:37,825
I am nothing.

1127
01:22:37,959 --> 01:22:40,228
We're only here
'cause you stole the heart

1128
01:22:40,360 --> 01:22:41,295
in the first place.

1129
01:22:41,428 --> 01:22:42,630
No.

1130
01:22:43,164 --> 01:22:44,565
We're here

1131
01:22:44,699 --> 01:22:47,902
because the ocean told you
that you were special.

1132
01:22:49,337 --> 01:22:50,638
And you believed it.

1133
01:22:52,006 --> 01:22:54,075
-I am Moana of Motunui.
-Goodbye, Moana.

1134
01:22:54,208 --> 01:22:56,409
You will sail across the sea
and restore the heart...

1135
01:22:56,544 --> 01:22:58,445
I'm not killing myself
so you can prove
you're something you're not.

1136
01:22:58,579 --> 01:23:01,949
The ocean chose me!
It chose us!

1137
01:23:03,117 --> 01:23:04,518
It chose wrong.

1138
01:23:05,452 --> 01:23:07,454
-Goodbye, Moana.
-Maui!

1139
01:23:17,198 --> 01:23:19,734
Maui, no! Don't go!

1140
01:23:28,475 --> 01:23:29,710
Maui?

1141
01:23:41,856 --> 01:23:44,457
Ocean, why did you
bring me here?

1142
01:23:46,961 --> 01:23:49,030
I was never the right person.

1143
01:23:54,635 --> 01:23:56,837
You should choose
someone else.

1144
01:23:59,173 --> 01:24:00,675
Please.

1145
01:24:02,276 --> 01:24:03,511
Please.

1146
01:25:25,259 --> 01:25:28,629
You're a long ways
past the reef.

1147
01:25:32,366 --> 01:25:33,534
Gramma.

1148
01:25:33,667 --> 01:25:37,104
I guess I chose
the right tattoo.

1149
01:25:50,885 --> 01:25:53,187
I tried, Gramma, but...

1150
01:25:53,654 --> 01:25:55,289
I couldn't do it.

1151
01:25:56,424 --> 01:25:57,892
I can't do it.

1152
01:25:58,893 --> 01:26:01,162
If you're ready to go home,

1153
01:26:01,295 --> 01:26:03,564
I will be with you.

1154
01:26:19,880 --> 01:26:22,583
Why do you hesitate?

1155
01:26:27,321 --> 01:26:28,422
I don't know.

1156
01:26:30,024 --> 01:26:33,060
♪ <i>I know a girl</i>
<i>From an island</i> ♪

1157
01:26:33,194 --> 01:26:36,430
♪ <i>She stands apart</i>
<i>From the crowd</i> ♪

1158
01:26:36,565 --> 01:26:40,167
♪ <i>She loves the sea</i>
<i>And her people</i> ♪

1159
01:26:40,301 --> 01:26:43,505
♪ <i>She makes</i>
<i>Her whole family proud</i> ♪

1160
01:26:43,637 --> 01:26:47,208
♪ <i>Sometimes the world</i>
<i>Seems against you</i> ♪

1161
01:26:47,341 --> 01:26:50,811
♪ <i>The journey</i>
<i>May leave a scar</i> ♪

1162
01:26:50,945 --> 01:26:53,180
♪ <i>But scars can heal</i>
<i>And reveal</i> ♪

1163
01:26:53,314 --> 01:26:56,684
♪ <i>Just where you are...</i> ♪

1164
01:26:58,085 --> 01:27:00,754
♪ <i>The people you love</i>
<i>Will change you</i> ♪

1165
01:27:00,888 --> 01:27:04,091
♪ <i>The things you have learned</i>
<i>Will guide you</i> ♪

1166
01:27:04,225 --> 01:27:07,596
♪ <i>And nothing on earth</i>
<i>Can silence</i> ♪

1167
01:27:07,728 --> 01:27:10,998
♪ <i>The quiet voice</i>
<i>Still inside you</i> ♪

1168
01:27:11,132 --> 01:27:14,768
♪ <i>And when that voice</i>
<i>Starts to whisper</i> ♪

1169
01:27:14,902 --> 01:27:18,072
♪ <i>"Moana, you've come so far"</i> ♪

1170
01:27:18,873 --> 01:27:20,774
♪ <i>Moana, listen...</i> ♪

1171
01:27:20,908 --> 01:27:25,846
♪ <i>Do you know who you are?</i> ♪

1172
01:27:28,617 --> 01:27:29,950
Who am I?

1173
01:27:32,419 --> 01:27:35,590
♪ <i>I am a girl</i>
<i>Who loves my island</i> ♪

1174
01:27:35,723 --> 01:27:39,126
♪ <i>And the girl</i>
<i>Who loves the sea</i> ♪

1175
01:27:40,529 --> 01:27:44,064
♪ <i>It calls me</i> ♪

1176
01:27:45,499 --> 01:27:48,469
♪ <i>I am the daughter</i>
<i>Of the village chief</i> ♪

1177
01:27:48,603 --> 01:27:51,640
♪ <i>We are descended</i>
<i>From voyagers</i> ♪

1178
01:27:51,772 --> 01:27:54,909
♪ <i>Who found their way</i>
